---
source: tests/ui/lint/mod.rs
---
  ▲ Compound assignment repeats `a`
   ╭─[test.lis:4:3]
 3 │   let mut a = 2
 4 │   a &= a & b
   ·   ─────┬────
   ·        ╰── uses `a` twice
 5 │   let _ = a
   ╰────
  help: To apply `b` once, write `a &= b`. The `&=` operator already includes `a`, so naming `a` again on the right applies it twice · code: [lint.misrefactored_assign_op]
